# KaamPay — Real-Time Chat & Notification System
## Implementation Plan (Beginner-Friendly, Step-by-Step)

> **Context:** Your project is a Next.js 16 + Express 5 monorepo with Prisma (PostgreSQL), Better-Auth, Cloudinary, Zustand, and TailwindCSS. The Prisma schema already has `ChatRoom`, `Message`, and `Notification` models. This plan builds on top of what exists.

---

## Architecture Overview

```
Browser (Client / Freelancer)
        │  Socket.io (WebSocket)
        ▼
Express Server ──── Kafka Producer ──── Aiven Kafka Broker
        │                                       │
        │                               Kafka Consumer
        │                                       │
        │                               Redis Stream
        │                                       │
        └── Socket.io ◄──── Redis Adapter ──────┘
                │
                ▼
         PostgreSQL (persist messages)
         Cloudinary (store files)
```

**The flow in plain English:**
1. User types a message and hits Send
2. Frontend emits `send_message` via Socket.io
3. Express receives it → pushes to **Aiven Kafka** topic
4. A Kafka consumer reads it → stores to **PostgreSQL** → puts it in **Redis Stream**
5. Socket.io (with Redis adapter) reads from Redis Stream → broadcasts to the other person's browser
6. Result: both users see the message in real-time

